 "chapters": [
  {
   "t": 1.4,
   "text": "SimVehicleApp: control a robot dog with a drag-and-drop workflow"
  },
  {
   "t": 2.8,
   "text": "1. Open SimVehicleApp and create an account"
  },
  {
   "t": 12.4,
   "text": "2. Create a workflow and name it"
  },
  {
   "t": 15.9,
   "text": "3. Toolbar → Signals: choose RSS (robot dog) — the palette now shows the robot blocks only"
  },
  {
   "t": 18.4,
   "text": "4. The robot's signals (RSS): e.g. Perception → Marker → IsDetected"
  },
  {
   "t": 21.4,
   "text": "5. Drag robot blocks from the Toolbar onto the canvas"
  },
  {
   "t": 29,
   "text": "6. Drag a robot signal onto the canvas → Wait until (the condition is filled in)"
  },
  {
   "t": 30.8,
   "text": "5. Drag robot blocks from the Toolbar onto the canvas"
  },
  {
   "t": 48.9,
   "text": "7. Set each block: conditions on RSS signals, motions, coordinates, log messages"
  },
  {
   "t": 74.2,
   "text": "8. Connect the named outputs: done / failed, then / else, loop / after loop"
  },
  {
   "t": 89.5,
   "text": "9. Problems: the RobotFlow compiler checks the workflow as you edit — no errors"
  },
  {
   "t": 91.1,
   "text": "10. Build: the compiler turns the workflow into a Python robot app (same input, same bytes)"
  },
  {
   "t": 92.9,
   "text": "11. Deploy to Dog ROS sim — binds the build to the robot; nothing runs yet"
  },
  {
   "t": 94.6,
   "text": "12. Robot Zoo opens in a new tab (the dog simulation, its own repository)"
  },
  {
   "t": 96.2,
   "text": "Robot Zoo: simulated Go2 dog (ROS 2 + MuJoCo), DISARMED"
  },
  {
   "t": 98.1,
   "text": "13. Start (with confirmation): the workflow drives the robot through RSS → Protobus → ROS 2"
  },
  {
   "t": 106.1,
   "text": "The robot follows the workflow: Arm → sees the marker → Bow → Lift paw → Jump → patrol twice"
  },
  {
   "t": 121.2,
   "text": "Studio, Live tab: the running block is outlined; each robot command with its result and request id"
  },
  {
   "t": 126.2,
   "text": "The robot follows the workflow: Arm → sees the marker → Bow → Lift paw → Jump → patrol twice"
  },
  {
   "t": 141.3,
   "text": "Studio, Live tab: the running block is outlined; each robot command with its result and request id"
  },
  {
   "t": 146.3,
   "text": "Robot Zoo, Logs & diagnostics: the robot's own ROS log of the same commands"
  },
  {
   "t": 156.9,
   "text": "The robot follows the workflow: Arm → sees the marker → Bow → Lift paw → Jump → patrol twice"
  },
  {
   "t": 156.9,
   "text": "14. Result: every command SUCCEEDED, the run finished by itself, the robot is DISARMED again"
  },
  {
   "t": 160,
   "text": "Done — Stop is always available in the studio and in Robot Zoo"
  }
 ],
